{"version":1,"content":"<html><body><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://pro-img-cdn.tvb.com/uploads/image/2026/11/20268584sYJyi31793701951.jpg?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_1200\"/><p>有調查發現，有旅客曾在香港旅遊時，出現嚴重食物過敏。</p><p></p><p>香港過敏科協會聯同多個機構，7月訪問逾200名有食物過敏的旅客，在港旅遊時有否不適。當中近四分之一、即逾50名受訪者，指試過在進食後，出現胃痛、偏頭痛等不適。當中3成更有嚴重或過敏性休克反應，但逾半旅客都無帶俗稱「救命針」的腎上腺素自動注射器。</p><p></p><p><p><img alt=\"Picture_J.ALLERGY-1630.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://pro-img-cdn.tvb.com/uploads/image/2026/11/2026xplqg6lBW21793702037.jpg?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_1200\"/></p></p><p></p><p>機構建議為餐飲及旅遊業界加強有關食物過敏的培訓，遇到突發情況時可協助。</p></body></html>","scraped_at":"2026-11-03T11:21:59.863788+00:00","quality":{"score":1,"chars":185,"images":2,"source":"TVB 新聞","fallback":"none","origin":"article-html","completeness":"extracted"},"published_at":"2026-11-03T09:18:00+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-11-03T12:59:06.860223+00:00","content_updated_at":"2026-11-03T11:18:44.532684+00:00","content_hash":"010787253e72c44b3e265b6933e47e235d9e33594ba83cb8adb53f0d55725c0a","evidence_status":"full","scrape_error":null,"content_retention":null,"content_capture":null}